<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer to cut 50 jobs at foundry unit.</title>
<headline>Sulzer to cut 50 jobs at foundry unit.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss engineering group Sulzer AG said on Wednesday it would cut 50 of 225 jobs at its  Sulzer Buehlachguss AG foundry unit due to a massive decline in demand since the beginning of the year.</p>
<p>Sulzer said in a statement that workers would change to single from double shifts to secure the unit's survival. The 50 workers will receive their notice of termination by end-year.</p>
<p>Sulzer said demand for small foundries had continued to drop this year and the output of foundries had fallen by one-third.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
